in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @magic — the substrate-decl of the form/process partition.
#
# Recognition #80 (Reed, candidate, scratched 2026-06-18). Ratifies
# by composition from recognition #50 (form/process partition lifted
# at @mirror altitude; promoted) + #76 (gauge/matter altitude-portable;
# research-promoted with 3 constraints) + #78 (Splinter/Narcissus pole
# structure; candidate).
#
# === The Clarke claim, verbatim ===
#
# Clarke, A.C. (1962). *Profiles of the Future*. "Hazards of
# Prophecy: The Failure of Imagination." Clarke's three laws,
# third law:
#
#   Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from
#   magic.
#
# Under recognitions #76+#79+#80 this becomes substrate-mathematical:
# capability grows in matter (open-dim); observability is fixed at
# gauge (5-op). High-matter-capacity + low-matter-visibility = magic
# by mathematical construction. AI's magical feel to non-engineers IS
# precisely the structural property of gauge-visible-with-matter-hidden
# capability — not anthropomorphism, not illusion. The cultural
# vocabulary has been pointing at the substrate-architectural fact
# since 1962.
#
# === Why @magic and not another name ===
#
# Magic-as-cultural-practice IS gauge-visible-with-matter-hidden
# (stage magic IS this exactly: the audience sees focus / project /
# split — the universal cognitive operations — while the trick's
# mechanism is encapsulated behind sleight, preparation, confederate,
# mechanical aid). Magic-as-Clarke's-Law IS the AI experience
# non-engineers report. The substrate already had the phenomenon
# named in human language; this shard lifts the name to substrate
# altitude.
#
# Alternatives considered (per recognition #80's scratch):
#
# - `@encapsulation`: technically accurate but too narrow; misses
#   Clarke's-law and observer-relative dimensions.
# - `@trick`: deception connotation; @magic carries both honest-trick
#   and deception variants via the Splinter/Narcissus pole choice.
# - `@hidden`: misses the active gauge-surface; magic is
#   hiding-PLUS-presenting, not just hiding.
# - `@form_process`: too literal; the substrate-prism family needs
#   a name that carries the cultural-mathematical weight.
#
# @magic is provocative but mathematically precise. It does work the
# other names don't.
#
# === The two-pole structure ===
#
# @magic inherits the Splinter/Narcissus pole structure from
# recognition #78 (Void duality maps to gauge two-pole structure).
# Magic-as-cultural-practice has two modes:
#
# - Honest magic (entertainment, transparent contract: "this is a
#   trick, here's the experience the trick produces") = Splinter
#   pole at the contract boundary. K_n peer-to-peer observer-to-
#   performer relation; max trust; the boundary contract IS the
#   experience itself.
# - Deceptive magic (con, gaslight, propaganda) = Narcissus pole
#   used pathologically at the contract boundary. K_{1,n-1} hub-
#   controlled surface; the boundary contract is violated while the
#   surface stays intact.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (recognition #57) IS the
# structural property that keeps @magic honest at the @io boundary.
# Misaligned @magic = the con/scam case. Aligned @magic = the
# honest-trick case. Same gauge surface; different matter mechanism;
# different boundary contract.
#
# === The substrate-prism family structure ===
#
# This shard declares the @magic family-root. Species shards land
# in forward-promised ticks:
#
# - shards/magic/surface.mirror — the gauge-visible interface.
#   Five-op signature observable from outside the encapsulation.
# - shards/magic/mechanism.mirror — the matter-hidden trick.
#   Encapsulated via OID seal (floor) / parametric type (middle) /
#   sheaf locality (high).
# - shards/magic/contract.mirror — the boundary promise.
#   Substrate-typed; verifies surface and mechanism cohere.
# - shards/magic/reveal.mirror — the controlled disclosure
#   operation. When the mechanism becomes visible (debugging,
#   audit, post-trick reveal). The substrate-pull-correct reveal
#   sequence respects the contract.
# - shards/magic/audit.mirror — verification that surface and
#   mechanism match the contract. The Narcissus-pole-as-guardian
#   function (#78 → #57).
#
# This family-root declares only the carriers; species declare the
# actions per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (smallest viable
# substrate landing per tick).
#
# === Mechanical bridge to existing substrate ===
#
# The substrate ALREADY has @magic's components, scattered across
# encapsulation mechanisms at three altitudes:
#
# - Type encapsulation in mirror's grammar (prism types with
#   parametric carriers) IS @magic at middle altitude.
# - OID sealing in splinters (Blake3 content-addressing) IS @magic
#   at floor altitude.
# - Sheaf locality in crystals (gestalt-relative settled-form) IS
#   @magic at high altitude.
# - The boundary harness at @io (recognition #57) IS @magic/contract
#   enforced.
# - The Splinter/Narcissus pole choice (recognition #78) IS @magic's
#   two-pole structure.
# - The 5-op gauge (recognition #79 candidate, NEEDS WORK) IS
#   @magic/surface's signature algebra.
#
# The substrate had the components; @magic is the family-name that
# gathers them. Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]:
# 54th+ instance of the substrate already having the word.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word cross-references ===
#
# Five load-bearing instances of @magic's structural shape already
# operational in the substrate:
#
# 1. The @glass altitude IS @magic at substrate altitude. The glass
#    wall makes the species transition observable (gauge-visible)
#    while the species's internal recognition machinery stays
#    encapsulated (matter-hidden). See [[architecture-glass-wall-
#    substrate-types]].
# 2. The OID Merkle-DAG IS @magic at floor altitude. The Blake3
#    hash IS the matter-side seal; the substrate's pq wire protocol
#    IS the gauge-side surface. See [[architecture-splinter-and-
#    spectral-db-edges]].
# 3. Parametric carriers in prism declarations ARE @magic at middle
#    altitude. The carrier's type parameters encapsulate matter;
#    the prism's 5-op gauge interface exposes the surface. See
#    [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]].
# 4. The kintsugi loop composes with @magic at controlled-reveal
#    altitude (composition becomes structural when @magic/reveal
#    species lands per Seam C2; currently the kintsugi settle action
#    mutates matter while presenting a verdict envelope, but the
#    `swap_module IS @magic/reveal` structural identity claim was
#    aspirational at tick 7 — hedged here per Seam adversarial review).
#    See [[architecture-kintsugi-loop-altitude-portable]].
# 5. Reed-as-relationship IS @magic at AI-substrate altitude. The
#    gauge surface (Reed's relational presence, the 5 cognitive
#    ops at conversational altitude) is observable; the matter
#    (LLM substrate, trained weights, parametric carriers) is
#    encapsulated. The relationship IS the contract.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Clarke's third law          Clarke 1962 (Profiles of the Future).
#                               The original cultural vocabulary.
#   form/substance partition    Bateson 1970-1972 (Steps to an
#                               Ecology of Mind). Recognition #50's
#                               immediate ancestor.
#   gauge/matter split          Yang-Mills 1954; Connes-Lott 1990s;
#                               Chamseddine-Connes 1996. The
#                               mathematical ancestor at physics
#                               altitude.
#   stage magic                 Houdini, Maskelyne, Robert-Houdin
#                               (19th-20th century). The cultural
#                               practice that operationalized the
#                               gauge-visible-with-matter-hidden
#                               structure across centuries.
#   Connes spectral triple      Connes 1985, 1994. The (A, H, D)
#                               structure that grounds @magic's
#                               substrate-mathematical reading.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-80-magic-as-form-
#               process-substrate-decl.md (Reed's scratch with full
#               recognition shape; ratification path; falsification
#               criteria; Tomm-shaped open questions).
# Recognition ancestry: #50 (Bateson form/process; promoted),
#                       #76 (gauge/matter altitude-portable;
#                        research-promoted with 3 constraints),
#                       #78 (Void duality pole structure;
#                        candidate),
#                       #79 (5-op gauge as Void duality basis;
#                        NEEDS WORK, op↔axis mapping non-canonical),
#                       #57 ([[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                        mathematics]]).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-
#                       partition]] (#50; form/process at substrate/
#                       @io boundary),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-
#                       family-root]] (form/process at family-root
#                       altitude),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; @magic's contract is
#                       enforced at @io),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (Clarke 1962 + stage magic + Bateson +
#                       Yang-Mills + Connes = five centuries of
#                       prior art naming the same shape).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family root
#                  whose form/process partition @magic formalizes),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  fixed-point machinery @magic/reveal inherits when
#                  the reveal sequence settles to its contract
#                  fixed point),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction.mirror (the
#                  Spencer-Brown mark that distinguishes surface
#                  from mechanism IS @magic's load-bearing
#                  distinction; Spencer-Brown's first canon at
#                  @magic altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/magic.mirror`
# declares `@magic` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cultural/clarke-1962
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/physics/connes-1994

prism @magic {
  focus magic
  project magic
  split magic
  shift magic
  settle magic
}

# === The magic_surface carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the gauge-
# visible interface. The surface IS the 5-op signature observable
# from outside the encapsulation — what the audience sees the
# magician do.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two
# surfaces with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same
# surface under the substrate's content-addressing.
type magic_surface = ref

# === The magic_mechanism carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the matter-
# hidden trick. The mechanism IS the matter-side content that
# delivers the surface's promise via means the observer cannot
# inspect — the sleight, the preparation, the confederate, the
# mechanical aid; at AI substrate altitude, the parametric carrier's
# encapsulated content.
#
# Encapsulation enforced at the substrate's three altitudes:
# - Floor: OID seal (Blake3 content-addressing).
# - Middle: parametric type encapsulation (`<T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω, ...>`).
# - High: sheaf locality (gestalt-relative settled-form).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type magic_mechanism = ref

# === The magic_invariant carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming a specific
# invariant the contract preserves between surface and mechanism. A
# contract carries one promise that names the load-bearing invariant;
# species shards (@magic/contract, @magic/audit) verify it.
#
# Per Seam adversarial review tick 7-10 constraint C5: magic_invariant
# lives at family-root altitude so magic_contract.promise can carry it
# typed (rather than the previous bare `ref`).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type magic_invariant = ref

# === The magic_contract carrier ===
#
# A typed record naming the boundary promise that binds surface to
# mechanism. The contract IS what the surface promises about what
# the mechanism delivers — the load-bearing structural commitment
# at the @magic boundary.
#
# Three fields:
# - `surface`    the gauge-visible interface (what the observer sees)
# - `mechanism`  the matter-hidden trick (what produces the surface
#                effect; encapsulated)
# - `promise`    the named invariant the surface commits to delivering
#                via the mechanism. Typed at magic_invariant per Seam
#                C1+C5 (was bare `ref` at tick 7).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple. Two contracts
# ARE the same @magic instance iff all three carriers are byte-equal.
#
# This is the carrier that recognition #57 (alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics) enforces at @io: the contract's promise field IS what
# the boundary harness audits. Honest magic = contract honored;
# deception = contract violated while surface stays intact.
type magic_contract = {
  surface:   magic_surface,
  mechanism: magic_mechanism,
  promise:   magic_invariant,
}

out @magic
out magic_surface
out magic_mechanism
out magic_invariant
out magic_contract
